{
  "id": "27776_nidasu",
  "headword": "{煮出|にだ}す",
  "reading": "にだす",
  "romaji": "nidasu",
  "part_of_speech": "verb (godan)",
  "gloss": "to brew; to boil to extract (flavor)",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to brew; to boil to extract (flavor)",
      "explanation": "To boil an ingredient in water to draw out its flavor, color, or active components, as when making stock, tea, or herbal infusions."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "27776_nidasu_ex1",
      "japanese": "⟦{昆布|こんぶ}→昆布：04934_konbu⟧でだし⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{煮出|にだ}す。",
      "english": "To boil kelp to make stock.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "27776_nidasu_ex2",
      "japanese": "⟦{麦茶|むぎちゃ}→麦茶：16494_mugicha⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{煮出|にだ}して⟦{冷|ひ}やす→冷やす：02403_hiyasu⟧。",
      "english": "I brew barley tea by boiling and then chill it.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "27776_nidasu_ex3",
      "japanese": "⟦{薬草|やくそう}→薬草：14033_yakusou⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧⟦じっくり→じっくり：06252_jikkuri⟧{煮出|にだ}す⟦と→と：00512_to⟧、⟦{独特|どくとく}→独特：01656_dokutoku⟧⟦の→の：09472_no⟧⟦{香|かお}り→香り：00189_kaori⟧⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧⟦{広|ひろ}がる→広がる：01980_hirogaru⟧。",
      "english": "When you slowly boil the herbs, a distinctive aroma spreads.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "TRANSITIVITY: Transitive godan verb. X⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{煮出|にだ}す. Compound of ⟦{煮|に}る→煮る：01971_niru⟧ (to boil) + ⟦{出|だ}す→出す：01087_dasu⟧ (to bring out). The ⟦{出|だ}す→出す：01087_dasu⟧ here means drawing the flavor out of the ingredient.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- だし⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{煮出|にだ}す: to boil out stock\n- ⟦お{茶|ちゃ}→お茶：00576_ocha⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{煮出|にだ}す: to brew tea by boiling\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- ⟦{煮込|にこ}む→煮込む：05822_nikomu⟧: to stew; to simmer — cooking the ingredient itself slowly, not extracting from it\n- ⟦{抽出|ちゅうしゅつ}する→抽出する：19627_chuushutsusuru⟧: to extract — a formal, technical term, not limited to boiling",
